  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Sum each of the following infinite geometric series:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{2^n}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$",
          "worked": "The first term is $a=\\frac12$ and the common ratio is $r=\\frac12$. Since $|r|<1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S&=\\frac{\\frac12}{1-\\frac12}\\\\S&=1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{2}{3^n}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$",
          "worked": "The first term is $a=\\frac23$ and the common ratio is $r=\\frac13$. Since $|r|<1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S&=\\frac{\\frac23}{1-\\frac13}\\\\S&=1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\left(\\frac34\\right)^n$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3$",
          "worked": "The first term is $a=\\frac34$ and the common ratio is $r=\\frac34$. Since $|r|<1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S&=\\frac{\\frac34}{1-\\frac34}\\\\S&=3.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{2^{n-1}}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$",
          "worked": "At $n=1$, the first term is $a=\\frac{1}{2^0}=1$. The common ratio is $r=\\frac12$. Since $|r|<1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S&=\\frac{1}{1-\\frac12}\\\\S&=2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q3-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{3}{4^{n-1}}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4$",
          "worked": "At $n=1$, the first term is $a=\\frac{3}{4^0}=3$. The common ratio is $r=\\frac14$. Since $|r|<1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S&=\\frac{3}{1-\\frac14}\\\\S&=4.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q3-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\left(\\frac35\\right)^{n-1}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac52$",
          "worked": "At $n=1$, the first term is $a=\\left(\\frac35\\right)^0=1$. The common ratio is $r=\\frac35$. Since $|r|<1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S&=\\frac{1}{1-\\frac35}\\\\S&=\\frac52.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      }
    ]
  },
